# Written by Settings → Colors (the sliders). Absent = these defaults.
#   CONTRAST_BIAS: where text flips light/dark over the colors.
#     0.5 = auto/default · 0 = always dark text · 1 = always light text.
#   SATURATION: mute/boost the wallpaper colors everywhere (bar + all apps).
#     0 = grayscale · 1 = as-extracted · >1 = boosted.
#   BRIGHTNESS: darken/lighten every color. 0 = black · 1 = as-extracted · 2 = brighter.
#   HUE: rotate every color around the wheel, in degrees. 0 = unchanged (-180..180).
CONTRAST_BIAS=0.5
SATURATION=1.0
BRIGHTNESS=1.0
HUE=0.0
#
# Per-surface tuning (Settings → Colors → Per-surface). Each surface layers its
# OWN sat/bright/hue ON TOP of the global knobs above. SAT/BRIGHT here are
# MULTIPLIERS (1.0 = unchanged, <1 tones that surface down, >1 boosts); HUE
# rotates (degrees). Keys: <SURFACE>_SAT / _BRIGHT / _HUE. Absent = unchanged.
# Surfaces: BAR NOTIFICATIONS GTK DISCORD SPOTIFY BRAVE KDE TELEGRAM.
# (KDE = Dolphin + other KF6/Qt apps via kdeglobals.) Example — tame Discord,
# brighten the bar:
#   DISCORD_SAT=0.7
#   BAR_BRIGHT=1.15
